-- title:
--   Minimal primes of the H₁ moduli ring contract to zero
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, an integer $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $(q\ell_g)$-th root of unity $\xi$, admitting a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\xi=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell_g)}$. Let $H_1\le(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell_g)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell_g$, and let $K\subseteq L(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ be the intermediate field generated over $L$ by the image, under coefficientwise extension along $\mathbb{Q}\to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_{H_1}$ of level $q^2M'$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ and $q$ in its maximal ideal, acting on $K$ compatibly, and let $j\in K$ be the element whose Laurent series is the base change of the $q$-expansion of $j$, assumed nonzero. Assume $\ell_g$ and $M'$ are units in $A$; assume the three equivariance hypotheses stating that the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point condition, the cyclic-kernel condition `IsGamma0PowAt` and divisibility of `inLineMulPoly` are preserved by variable changes over arbitrary $A$-algebras; let $\mathcal{G}$ be a family of relative group laws on the projective Weierstrass models over $A$-algebras which is chord–tangent and has the origin as identity, and $\mathcal{T}$ a level transport for $\mathcal{G}$ at $q$ satisfying `IsSectionTransport`; assume, for all $A$-algebras, the existence of graded ring maps realising variable changes (`IsVariableChangeHom`) and coefficient maps (`IsCoefficientHom`) compatibly with the irrelevant ideals. Let $P_0$ be an absolute moduli package for the rigid Weierstrass data `rigidDataH1Pow` (a $\Gamma_0(M')$-kernel tuple together with a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point, linked by `IsGamma1Link`, together with Drinfeld level-$q$ structure), so that $B_0=P_0.B_0$ carries a universal point representing the functor, and assume $B_0$ is of finite type over $A$. Then for every minimal prime $\mathfrak p$ of the zero ideal of $B_0$, the contraction of $\mathfrak p$ along the inclusion of the $A$-subalgebra generated by `P₀.j₀` into $B_0$ is the zero ideal.
--
--   This is the statement that every irreducible component of the fine moduli ring of the $H_1$-level problem dominates the $j$-line: no minimal prime of $B_0$ meets the subalgebra $A[j_0]$ nontrivially. It feeds the counts of minimal primes and the identification of the components of $B_0$ with Galois conjugates of the function field $K$.
